# _switch_off_walled_account: does a wall 429 on /v1/messages become a 401?
#
# THE DECISION, not the code path. Every parameter below is an input the
# function reads; the outcome is exactly one of {relay the 429, answer 401}
# plus whether claude-swap's switch() was called at all. A relayed WALL 429
# (ResetHeader=Present) is no longer byte-identical: its rate-limit headers
# are stripped before it leaves. An Absent-reset relay is untouched.
#
# Why a model and not a list of cases: an unrun gate reads like a passed one,
# and a hand-written suite has that property one level down. A required pair
# with no case is a HOLE; a case outside the model is REDUNDANT. Measured in
# this seam: replacing the bearer path's expiry call with `(False, None)` left
# all 38 hand-written cases green while starving a straggler the docstring
# promises to serve -- a combination nobody had imagined, leaving no trace of
# its absence.
#
# Expand:  pict tests/models/at_limit_conversion.pict
# Syntax:  https://github.com/microsoft/pict

# The wall's own anthropic-ratelimit-unified-reset. Empty means this is not an
# account-level unified wall (edge/gateway, or org/key-scoped).
ResetHeader: Present, Absent

# _walled_switch_seen[(reset, slot)] when this 429 arrives. The key is the pair
# because a reset epoch is a CLOCK BOUNDARY two accounts can share.
MemoEntry: Unseen, SettledConversion, LiveNegative, ExpiredNegative

# The Authorization value the pin forwarded upstream. /v1/messages is never a
# pinned route, so this is the client's own bearer.
Authorization: BearerStale, BearerIsLive, NonBearerScheme, NoHeader

# _active_oauth_token(): the live account's access token, or None.
LiveToken: Readable, Unreadable

# current_account_number(): the live slot, or None for an unmanaged login.
LiveSlot: Managed, Unmanaged

# _live_account_headroom(slot). Ample/Hairline are (0,100]; Exhausted is
# exactly 0.0 and OverLimit is negative. The last four are UNKNOWN and must be
# indistinguishable from one another at the call site.
Headroom: Ample, Hairline, Exhausted, OverLimit, NoReading, Sentinel, MissingBaseWindow, ScopedOnly

# What claude-swap's switch() does, when it is reached at all.
Switch: LandedValidated, LandedUnvalidated, NoCandidate, NeedsLogin, Raised

# THREE-WAY, FOR THESE THREE ONLY. The identity test is a three-condition
# guard (`token and live and slot is not None`), and pairwise leaves its
# conditions co-varying: the sole Present row carrying a stale bearer with an
# unmanaged slot ALSO carried an unreadable token, so whichever guard fires
# first masked the other and deleting `slot is not None` left the sweep green.
# Order 3 over exactly this triple forces the isolating rows to exist.
{ Authorization, LiveToken, LiveSlot } @ 3

# --- constraints: combinations the code cannot present ---

# An absent reset returns at the top, before the memo and before every read
# below it, so those parameters are MASKED. Pin all of them: left free, the
# expansion spends 16 of 64 rows on one assertion AND parks real pairs there --
# (BearerStale, Unmanaged) and (BearerStale, Unreadable) landed only on an
# Absent row, so the sweep never reached the `slot is not None` and `live`
# guards those pairs exist to exercise. A pair covered only in a masked row is
# the HOLE this file's header is about.
IF [ResetHeader] = "Absent" THEN [MemoEntry] = "Unseen" AND [Authorization] = "BearerStale"
   AND [LiveToken] = "Readable" AND [LiveSlot] = "Managed" AND [Switch] = "NoCandidate";

# A live memo entry returns before the bearer test and before switch().
IF [MemoEntry] IN {"SettledConversion", "LiveNegative"} THEN [Switch] = "NoCandidate";

# Headroom is only READ once the identity test passes: a stale bearer, a
# readable live token, and a managed live slot. Pinned otherwise so the model
# does not enumerate a reading nobody takes.
IF NOT ([Authorization] = "BearerStale" AND [LiveToken] = "Readable" AND [LiveSlot] = "Managed")
   THEN [Headroom] = "Ample";
